  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1105 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nThe upper level low will remain over Middle TN on Tuesday keeping\nshower and thunderstorm chances in the forecast for the afternoon\nand early evening. The higher chances will favor the eastern half\nof the area. CAPE profiles will remain similar keeping the \nthunder chances overall low. The upper level low will get swept \nback into the flow on Wednesday as a trough digs into the Great \nLakes. Low rain chances will linger over the Plateau Wednesday \nafternoon and evening. Weak troughing then lingers over the region\nthrough the week into the weekend. This will keep low shower and \nthunderstorm chances in the forecast. CAPE values will increase \nas the week goes on and that will increase the thunderstorm \nchances but we will lack shear keeping the chance for strong \nstorms very low. Highs gradually warm throughout the week warming \nback into the mid to upper 80s by mid-week and into the upper 80s \nto lower 90s by the end of the week.",
